Vulkan encode: accept RGB input via VK_VALVE_video_encode_rgb_conversion

When the input frames are RGB (e.g. X2BGR10) and the device supports
VK_VALVE_video_encode_rgb_conversion, the encoder converts them to YCbCr
itself: the profile chains VkVideoEncodeProfileRgbConversionInfoVALVE,
the session chains VkVideoEncodeSessionRgbConversionCreateInfoVALVE
(model, range and chroma siting from the codec context), the input
picture format is the RGB format and the DPB uses the coded 4:2:0 format
(NV12 for 8-bit input, P010 for 10-bit). Headers are written for the
coded format (FFHWBaseEncodeContext.coded_sw_format).

This saves the separate RGB->YUV pass on the GPU's shader cores.

